    "text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.1</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is released from a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> on a curved smooth surface. On the horizontal surface, path <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AB</mi></math> is smooth and path <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>BC</mi></math>&nbsp;is rough with a coefficient of friction <math><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></math>. If the impact of the block with the vertical wall at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;is perfectly elastic, the total distance covered by the block on the horizontal surface before coming to rest will be (take <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>)<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/348114.JPG\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 116px;\" />",
